prompt_template:
The current directory is a checkout of the abapGit repository (ABAP sources in abapGit file format under src/). Read the method {method}, implemented in {file}, and list every method called directly in its body, with the line of each call. These count as method calls: receiver->name( ), class=>name( ), zif_x~name( ) and a bare name( ) of the class's own or inherited methods, in any position (a statement, an expression, a string template); CALL METHOD with a static name; and object creation with NEW or CREATE OBJECT, which is a call of constructor, as is super->constructor( ). A chained call a( )->b( ) is two calls. These do not count: function modules (CALL FUNCTION), PERFORM, dynamic calls whose method name is a literal or a variable (CALL METHOD (lv_name), ->('NAME')), built-in functions such as lines( ), strlen( ), to_lower( ) or xsdbool( ), constructor operators (VALUE, CONV, COND, SWITCH, REF, CAST, CORRESPONDING, EXACT, REDUCE, FILTER), RAISE EXCEPTION TYPE, statements such as CLEAR, anything in a comment, and calls inside the class's local test classes, which are not part of the method. Give each callee as written in the source (lo_x->name, zcl_x=>name, zif_x~name or name; constructor for an object creation) and the 1-based line number of the line where the called method's name appears. A method called several times is listed once per call.

End your reply with a single JSON object and nothing after it:
{{"calls": [{{"callee": "...", "line": 123}}]}}
